er.\n\nReason:\nPlaying ♦6 is the optimal move because:\n1. It\'s the minimum card needed to beat ♠5, conserving stronger cards\n2. It supports my teammate\'s strategy of playing low cards\n3. It forces the landlord to either waste a card or pass, giving us control\n4. I preserve my triplet of Aces, King, and mid-range cards for crucial plays later\n5. This maintains pressure on the landlord while being economical\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦6"]}'}
